# Combined QA + Archify wake (all projects)

Kit home: `~/Documents/Cursor-kits/`  
(Legacy: `~/Documents/QA-kit` + `~/Documents/Archify-kit`)

## One wake = QA + Archify + Live Guide

When the user says:

> make a apk release build and wake up the QA agent

You MUST (do **not** ask; do **not** require a second Archify command):

1. Resolve both roots:
   ```bash
   eval "$(bash ~/Documents/Cursor-kits/tools/resolve-roots.sh "$(pwd)")"
   echo "$QA_ROOT" "$ARCHIFY_ROOT"
   ```
2. Build release + run QA (`$QA_ROOT/agents/00-orchestrator.md` or qa-kit orchestrator).
3. **Automatically** attach Archify:
   ```bash
   ARCHIFY_ROOT=$(bash ~/Documents/Cursor-kits/tools/ensure-archify-with-qa.sh "$(pwd)")
   ```
   Run Archify orchestrator / plan — **you decide agent count**. Never ask the user how many agents.
4. After QA (+ Archify) finish, **always** open Live Guide:
   ```bash
   bash ~/Documents/Cursor-kits/tools/after-qa-open-live.sh "$ARCHIFY_ROOT" "<run_id-if-any>"
   ```

Only skip Archify if the user message contains `skip_archify: true`.

## Debug screen wake

> wake up the agent and QA this screen and its widgets (FILE) (WHAT_TO_QA)

Run screen QA, ensure Archify root exists, then open Live Guide when done.

## Hard rules

- Never edit product app source for QA or Archify
- Never tell the user to run “Make the archify of this project” after a QA wake — it is already included
- Write QA results only under `$QA_ROOT/results` + `reports`
- Write Archify under `$ARCHIFY_ROOT`
